/*Q27. You are developing an Invoice Management System for a hardware store. The system must store invoice details, validate the purchased
quantity and price, and calculate the total invoice amount.
Create a class named Invoice with the following instance variables:
• partNumber (String): stores the part number.
• partDescription (String): stores the description of the part.
• quantity (int): stores the number of items purchased.
• pricePerlItem (double): stores the price of one item.
Constructor
Implement a parameterized constructor Invoice(String partNumber, String partDescription, int quantity, double pricePerlItem) to initialize
all four instance variables.
The constructor must use setQuantity() and setPricePerItem() to validate the quantity and price.
Methods
Implement the following methods in the Invoice class:
• setQuantity(int quantity): Assigns the quantity if it is positive; otherwise, sets it to 0.
• getQuantity(): Returns the current quantity (int).
• setPricePerltem(double pricePerlItem): Assigns the price if it is positive; otherwise, sets it to 0.0.
• getPricePerltem(): Returns the current price per item (double).
• getPartNumber(): Returns the part number (String).
• getPartDescription(): Returns the part description (String).
• getInvoiceAmount(): Returns the total invoice amount (double) using the formula:
Invoice Amount = quantity * pricePerItem
The InvoiceTest class should read the invoice details, create an Invoice object, and display the invoice information and calculated amount
using the provided getter methods.
Input Format:
• The first line contains a string representing the Part Number.
• The second line contains a string representing the Part Description.
• The third line contains an integer representing the Quantity.
• The fourth line contains a double representing the Price per Item.
Output Format:
• For each invoice, display:
Part Number: <part_number>
Part Description: <part_description>
Quantity: <quantity>
Price per Item: <price_per_item>
Total Invoice Amount: <invoice_amount>
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
class Invoice {
    private String partNumber;
    private String partDescription;
    private int quantity;
    private double pricePerItem;
 
    Invoice(String partNumber, String partDescription, int quantity, double pricePerItem) {
        this.partNumber = partNumber;
        this.partDescription = partDescription;
        setQuantity(quantity);
        setPricePerItem(pricePerItem);
    }
 
    void setQuantity(int quantity) { this.quantity = quantity > 0 ? quantity : 0; }
    int getQuantity() { return quantity; }
    void setPricePerItem(double pricePerItem) {
        this.pricePerItem = pricePerItem > 0 ? pricePerItem : 0.0;
    }
    double getPricePerItem() { return pricePerItem; }
    String getPartNumber() { return partNumber; }
    String getPartDescription() { return partDescription; }
    double getInvoiceAmount() { return quantity * pricePerItem; }
}
 
public class InvoiceTest {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String num = sc.nextLine().trim();
        String desc = sc.nextLine().trim();
        int qty = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
        double price = Double.parseDouble(sc.nextLine().trim());
        Invoice inv = new Invoice(num, desc, qty, price);
        System.out.println("Part Number: " + inv.getPartNumber());
        System.out.println("Part Description: " + inv.getPartDescription());
        System.out.println("Quantity: " + inv.getQuantity());
        System.out.println("Price per Item: " + inv.getPricePerItem());
        System.out.println("Total Invoice Amount: " + inv.getInvoiceAmount());
        sc.close();
    }
}
